      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DAMAS (6) gets the nod after a fifth in Quality grade at Port Macquarie where he was keen early and hampered late, beaten only a length and a half. His prior third in a BM74 at the same venue was sound, and his record around 1120m gives him the right profile to rebound strongly. RICH STAR (5) is the clear danger on consistency, having been placed at all four starts this campaign and beaten just under a length in Class 3 company at both recent runs. Weight relief helps from the low draw. SISTINE EXPLORER (9) has not fired in two runs back, but third-up fitness, wet-track form and weight relief keep her in the winning mix if she improves sharply. DUNE AND DUSTED (7) has been competitive in BM66 grade, including a close fourth at this venue last start, and the big weight drop gives him a genuine place-to-win platform despite the rise in grade.",
